{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2545 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "607c3f8e414139686e1d10204464745b63d6efee0b33c309d8ddc57e3dae6225" :edb/db-before-t 2544 :edb/db-after-t 2545 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535857 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:06:17.638Z" 13194139535857 true] [17592186197985 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/0405639a97f249bbcc4dc18a7eae5b4df24aefb4b4680b569365b3d841c15e6b.png)\n\n   \n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\dfrac{y}2$ and $x=y-2$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda(x,y) =\\dfrac y8.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186197985 1100 "A plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\dfrac{y}2$ and $x=y-2$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda(x,y) =\\dfrac y8$. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/11eed00af0f2d1ea5c3dd9df00a40291.png)" 13194139535857 false] [17592186197985 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\:\\: 2x \\leq y \\leq x+2 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/3888077dfe4169493752346eb2247621.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = \\mid x - 2 \\mid\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)[r(x, y)]^{2}dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{2x}^{x + 2}(\\frac{y}{8}) \\mid x - 2 \\mid ^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{2x}^{x + 2}(\\frac{y}{8})(x - 2)^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(x - 2)^{2}∫_{2x}^{x + 2}\\frac{y}{8}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(x - 2)^{2}[\\frac{y^{2}}{16}]_{2x}^{x + 2}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}∫_{0}^{2}(x - 2)^{2}((x + 2)^{2} - (2x)^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}∫_{0}^{2}(x^{2} - 4x + 4)(4 + 4x - 3x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}∫_{0}^{2}(16 - 24x^{2} + 16x^{3} - 3x^{4})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}[16x - 8x^{3} + 4x^{4} - \\frac{3x^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}(32 - 64 + 64 - \\frac{96}{5}) - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}(\\frac{64}{5}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 false] [17592186197985 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\:\\: 2x \\leq y \\leq x+2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/69dcf02cc1883f2b04f81bd6dd486bbe24fedbb813db5778ae3b33ed1fb42e90.png)\n\n     \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}\\frac{y}{8}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}]}_{2x}^{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}((x+2)^{2}-(2x)^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(4+4x-3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(16-24{x}^{2}+16{x}^{3}-3{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{[16x-8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4}-\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(32-64+64-\\frac{96}{5})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(\\frac{64}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186197986 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/67d511da69c49e77822011936522f2b236ccc0fa0e0fcd09ce26b428cc8f738a.png)\n\n \n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y=x$ and $y=4x-x^2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\dfrac92$ square units, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186197986 1100 "A plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y=x$ and $y=4x-x^2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\dfrac92$ square units, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/b0b9a3962cb0c3c1dde403ebea8607ff.png)" 13194139535857 false] [17592186197986 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: x \\leq y \\leq 4x-x^2 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/03b423d9e4de7171ae11eedbfe4af11d.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = \\mid x - 3 \\mid\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2M}{9}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)[r(x, y)]^{2}dA \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}∫_{x}^{4x - x^{2}} \\mid x - 3 \\mid ^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}∫_{x}^{4x - x^{2}}(x - 3)^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}(x - 3)^{2}[y]_{y = x}^{y = 4x - x^{2}}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}(x^{2} - 6x + 9)(3x - x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3} - x^{4} + 9x^{3} - 27x^{2} + 27xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}[- \\frac{x^{5}}{5} + \\frac{9x^{4}}{4} - 9x^{3} + \\frac{27x^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{3^{2}}(-\\frac{3^{5}}{5} + \\frac{3^{6}}{4} - 3^{5} + \\frac{3^{5}}{2}) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3^{3}M(-\\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{3}{4} - 1 + \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{27M}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 false] [17592186197986 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: x \\leq y \\leq 4x-x^2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/6291950b5483f3c102df7249674412c7c11646409cb1b43df604de6bd5ace86f.png)\n\n  \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 3|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[y]_{y=x}^{y=4x-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-6x+9)(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}-{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-27{x}^{2}+27x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{9{x}^{4}}{4}-9{x}^{3}+\\frac{27{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{{3}^{2}}(-\\frac{{3}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{3}^{6}}{4}-{3}^{5}+\\frac{{3}^{5}}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{3}M(-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{3}{4}-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186197988 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/8ec9b8832f3286032413c4016e88a58a593dfd1b32164e219dc1c2e56e3b0b97.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt x$ and the line $x=1,$ as shown above. \nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-1.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186197988 1100 "A plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt x$ and the line $x=1$, as shown above.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/edc9cb439dea888f2ce37f4d8ad17b5c.png)" 13194139535857 false] [17592186197988 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/37d6c9a2f0b721457fa666b86f4e9c8d.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = \\begin{vmatrix}x-(-1) & = & x+1\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k \\mid y \\mid = ky\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}kydydx \\\\\n&= k∫_{0}^{1}[\\frac{1}{2}y^{2}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{2}∫_{0}^{1}(x - 0)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{2}∫_{0}^{1}xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{2} \\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}x^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k y = 4M y\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{l} &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)[r(x, y)]^{2}dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My \\mid x + 1 \\mid ^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My(x + 1)^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= 4M∫_{0}^{1}(x + 1)^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}ydydx \\\\\n&= 4M∫_{0}^{1}(x + 1)^{2}[\\frac{1}{2}y^{2}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}dx \\\\\n&= 2M∫_{0}^{1}(x + 1)^{2}(x - 0)dx \\\\\n&= 2M∫_{0}^{1}(x^{3} + 2x^{2} + x)dx \\\\\n&= 2M[\\frac{1}{4}x^{4} + \\frac{2}{3}x^{3} + \\frac{1}{2}x^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= 2M(\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= 2M \\cdot \\frac{17}{12} \\\\\n&= \\frac{17M}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 false] [17592186197988 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/7faaecf39250dbdd1b92d789f6c217afe883c27533b563dae82ed82d228d9b4d.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x-(-1)| = |x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda(x,y) = k |y| = ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k y = 4M y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My\\,|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2M(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2M\\cdot \\frac{17}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186198342 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370601 13194139535857 true] [17592186198342 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370608 13194139535857 true] [17592186198342 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370615 13194139535857 true] [17592186198342 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370622 13194139535857 true] [17592186198342 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370629 13194139535857 true] [17592186198343 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370636 13194139535857 true] [17592186198343 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370643 13194139535857 true] [17592186198343 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370650 13194139535857 true] [17592186198343 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370657 13194139535857 true] [17592186198345 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370664 13194139535857 true] [17592186198345 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370671 13194139535857 true] [17592186198345 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370678 13194139535857 true] [17592186198345 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370685 13194139535857 true] [17592186198575 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535857 true] [17592186198575 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/ed4f595e7613254fd0cb8f27cf0b0f7443cfbe382ab525b0ca8d527c07f528fd.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x}$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{3},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=1.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186198575 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/q-163000.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y = x^{2}$ and $y = \\sqrt{x}$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{3}$, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x = 1$." 13194139535857 false] [17592186198575 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/60ec523346df73503dd61893994de6ec31069271b1157f153bbe988c9e694798.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=3M.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-2x+1)(\\sqrt{x}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5/2}-2{x}^{3/2}+{x}^{1/2}-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{[\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{7/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3M(\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186198577 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535857 true] [17592186198577 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/b48e086ae0e94589d557eceb25b50af9deffdec442cfb7a4e559577bce899c40.png)\n\nA triangular plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $y=2x.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-2.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186198577 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/q-163008.png)\n\nA triangular plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $x$-axis and the lines $x = 1$ and $y = 2x$.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x =-2$." 13194139535857 false] [17592186198577 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/f040a5500a1415b8617300f34074bb16d895889354ed7e722dbd668a233daebb.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-(-2)|=|x+2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{3M}{2}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\frac{3M}{2}y\\,|x+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\frac{3M}{2}y(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5}+2{x}^{4}+\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}[\\frac{2}{5}+2+\\frac{8}{3}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}[\\frac{76}{15}] \\\\  & =\\frac{38M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370601 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370602 13194139535857 true] [17592186370601 1089 "q-163493" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370601 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535857 true] [17592186370601 1100 "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y-1$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370601 1113 #uuid "9142e89b-aec1-5dd7-a7d7-0241424a0791" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370601 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y-1)|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-2+y+1)(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-2)^{3}+(y+1)(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{[y(x-2)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(y+1)^{2}(x-2)^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(x-2)^{3}+\\frac{3}{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x-2)^{4}}{4}+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370603 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370604 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370605 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370606 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370607 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1041 "selection" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370606 13194139535857 true] [17592186370602 1110 #uuid "a8895096-5013-5ba6-bd94-b5c5d5f42e4d" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370603 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370603 1111 #uuid "3cee96a7-25db-5e03-91f4-56d41c2d4209" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370604 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [1759