ia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}(\\frac{y-1}{9})|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}(\\frac{y-1}{9})(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}\\frac{y-1}{9}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}{[\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{18}]}_{x+1}^{7-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[\\frac{(6-x)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[\\frac{12(3-x)}{18}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{(x-3)^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0-\\frac{81}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370631 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370632 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370633 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370634 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370635 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1041 "selection" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370631 13194139535857 true] [17592186370630 1110 #uuid "c85fb12f-bfd2-5441-8a86-b4002fe1b771" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370631 1034 "\\frac{27}{2}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370631 1111 #uuid "0c23a9e7-b376-5ce9-903d-f22766627096" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370632 1034 "\\frac{19}{2}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370632 1111 #uuid "c76e175b-53cf-5e26-8966-092d7c830164" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370633 1034 "\\frac{21}{2}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370633 1111 #uuid "a358a54d-ab57-5f14-9ef4-cd468cadcd51" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370634 1034 "30" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370634 1111 #uuid "333ec966-5d0f-5191-99cd-c33b62ea108c" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370635 1034 "29" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370635 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370635 1111 #uuid "abf82ae9-0a77-5908-8c1a-d784a1597a6f" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370636 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370637 13194139535857 true] [17592186370636 1089 "q-163618" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370636 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535857 true] [17592186370636 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=2.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370636 1113 #uuid "f82c33cd-5fdb-59d6-9b46-1e4b0a7ea3b9" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370636 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{M}{4}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{M}{4}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}\\cdot [x]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y-2)^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}(1-(-1))(\\frac{1}{3}(2-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(0-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(0-(-\\frac{8}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370638 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370639 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370640 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370641 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370642 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1041 "selection" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370640 13194139535857 true] [17592186370637 1110 #uuid "c1a9dfc7-f4f2-5493-9e2c-a92510fa6ecd" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370638 1034 "\\frac{5M}{3}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370638 1111 #uuid "b3240086-930e-549a-8cf1-87e6407cc50b" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370639 1034 "\\frac{5M}{6}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370639 1111 #uuid "89a916b5-917f-5c55-8ff7-b8aa2e4acf5b" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370640 1034 "\\frac{4M}{3}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370640 1111 #uuid "46c09183-8852-59da-86e9-88e0746cba5c" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370641 1034 "\\frac{2M}{3}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370641 1111 #uuid "6a98bf1a-90a9-56b9-ad86-e6e25d82b031" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370642 1034 "\\frac{M}{3}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370642 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370642 1111 #uuid "a0918678-451c-5145-acf5-427161556a78" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370644 13194139535857 true] [17592186370643 1089 "q-163621" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370643 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535857 true] [17592186370643 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370643 1113 #uuid "d1bd5086-46a3-54e4-b28e-039af25e92e4" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370643 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 1=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}({\\int }_{2}^{5}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x-2)^{3}]_{2}^{5}\\cdot {[y]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}(5-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(2-2)^{3})\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(9-0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370645 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370646 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370647 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370648 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370649 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1041 "selection" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370647 13194139535857 true] [17592186370644 1110 #uuid "4b953e83-5ff4-5294-9290-1242fb7643bf" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370645 1034 "\\frac{M}{2}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370645 1111 #uuid "183f20e3-d2cd-5e5a-91c0-082547219098" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370646 1034 "M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370646 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370646 1111 #uuid "55957380-5df5-5871-ac1a-67c48e9145bd" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370647 1034 "3M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370647 1111 #uuid "d45ebd6c-1645-5abd-ab4a-232926879b42" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370648 1034 "2M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370648 1111 #uuid "fdcc0e5c-9e20-5e1e-a14b-a7680825deb2" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370649 1034 "\\frac{5M}{4}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370649 1111 #uuid "e903cf5f-a042-5e9c-872c-0cec3cbeb4de" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370650 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370651 13194139535857 true] [17592186370650 1089 "q-163622" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370650 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535857 true] [17592186370650 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=-1.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370650 1113 #uuid "15faa565-0737-5b72-a4a0-6585bf2a9f39" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370650 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}({\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x+1)^{3}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(\\frac{1}{3}(2+1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(-1+1)^{3})\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(9-0)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370652 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370653 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370654 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370655 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370656 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1041 "selection" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370654 13194139535857 true] [17592186370651 1110 #uuid "f84654cf-b7ae-570b-909f-e6cdb3e736e4" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370652 1034 "M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370652 1111 #uuid "ec9c4051-ca46-592f-80e2-03065ca2892f" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370653 1034 "4M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370653 1111 #uuid "c00efc82-ed21-5811-bca6-9652882403b6" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370654 1034 "3M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370654 1111 #uuid "07377844-a68e-5bb4-8f82-91921c7e5f80" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370655 1034 "5M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370655 1111 #uuid "c4ad27b4-8a7e-54c8-83b3-352cba08164b" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370656 1034 "2M" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370656 1111 #uuid "fe1578c8-a801-5bc5-bdf6-b022af24e92b" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370658 13194139535857 true] [17592186370657 1089 "q-163626" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370657 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535857 true] [17592186370657 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/cd19503a1b72cd353cd2bacad0c187a1f83881d511b6ffcf0e99755ab9f682a9.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=x$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{4},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=1.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370657 1113 #uuid "dddb03a6-92c6-5454-bdcf-1c33144360e4" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370657 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/4463119c9f2ff0c1c658dd573add51a000cc50187e7dd59f39a40ba7c3abfce2.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=4M.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-2x+1)(x-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-2{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4}-{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4M(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370659 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370660 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370661 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370662 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370663 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1041 "selection" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370661 13194139535857 true] [17592186370658 1110 #uuid "1c9af981-1610-50e9-8c37-71c6b96a8dab" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370659 1034 "\\frac{M}{2}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370659 1111 #uuid "9d3b01e9-7201-5297-8a14-6bf87c905b8f" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370660 1034 "\\frac{4M}{7}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370660 1111 #uuid "e2d72ec7-9238-574e-867a-32ec5502fcaa" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370661 1034 "\\frac{4M}{15}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370661 1111 #uuid "0f47fdde-671e-5e73-b947-458c5c33c2af" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370662 1034 "\\frac{3M}{5}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370662 1111 #uuid "d7a2caaf-a09f-53e1-a943-0caaf613017e" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370663 1034 "\\frac{5M}{7}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370663 1111 #uuid "ed9f389f-757d-51b5-8ad7-3aaefbe8e921" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370664 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370665 13194139535857 true] [17592186370664 1089 "q-163656" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370664 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535857 true] [17592186370664 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its $x$-coordinate. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=-1.$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370664 1113 #uuid "04daaed1-6376-5a28-ad01-61618bc0bbd7" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370664 1145 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $y=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=kx,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =k(2-0)(3-0) \\\\  & =6k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=\\frac{M}{6}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{6}x|y+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{6}x(y+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}({\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}(y+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y+1)^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(4-0)\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(64-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\frac{63}{3} \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370666 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370667 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370668 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370669 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370670 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1041 "selection" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370668 13194139535857 true] [17592186370665 1110 #uuid "39bef840-01c9-5a46-b90f-558e659b455d" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370666 1034 "\\frac{64M}{9}" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535857 true] [17592186370666 1111 #uuid "95699bc2-35e0-55b1-b6ca-50dc7d18df04" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370667