on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/84ec89a3f4d786fe387b33aacc3de7c013866387354897f785ff69f9d65437ad.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $y=0$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y]}_{x/2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=8M{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}8M{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{x/2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{24})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7{x}^{5}}{24}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7{x}^{5}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{18}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535857 true] [17592186370679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370680 13194139535857 true] [17592186370679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370681 13194139535857 true] [17592186370679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370682 1319413